    {
      "id": "wikipedia-article-node-notes",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Concept Notes",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 775.6655484919305,
        "y": 609.7828978276902
      },
      "width": 620,
      "height": 420,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "wikipedia-article-node"
        },
        "markdown": "# Wikipedia Article Node\n\nThe node should preserve **source identity** separately from any cached presentation. A user should be able to point the node at a Wikipedia article and get a compact icon, useful summary, richer detail, and an editor that exposes source/refetch behavior.\n\nThe interesting product question is whether this is merely an embed, or a real semantic node that can expose article metadata, sections, references, images, links, and freshness as graph-addressable data.\n\nA strong version should remain inspectable and useful even when offline or when the upstream article changes.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1787160191065,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
